    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & -7 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $2$ pivots in the $2$nd and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & -7 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
